Limbo Android compatibility patch for QEMU 11.0.3

Apply from the QEMU source root:

    cd limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni/qemu
    patch -p1 < ../patches/qemu-11.0.3.patch

Two kinds of change live in here:

  1. Android/bionic build fixes -- QEMU upstream does not target Android, so
     a handful of macro collisions and missing-libc-feature issues have to be
     resolved before it compiles at all.

  2. Limbo integration -- the emulator has to be produced as a shared library
     that the app dlopen()s (Android forbids exec'ing binaries from an app's
     private directory), and a few display/audio knobs have to become runtime
     variables so the Java UI can tune them.

Every hunk is guarded so that a normal, non-Android build of QEMU is
unaffected: the build-system changes sit behind the new -Dshared_emulator
meson option or behind a probe for bionic, and the integration changes sit
behind #ifdef __LIMBO__.

Several hunks from Limbo's old qemu-5.1.0.patch are deliberately NOT carried
over, because upstream fixed the problem or deleted the code:

  exec.c limbo_ignore_breakpoint_invalidate  breakpoint_invalidate() is gone
  monitor/misc.c fd lookup bypass            Limbo does not use fdset/getfd
  ui/sdl2.c NULL console guard               QEMU 11 already checks !scon
  ui/sdl2.c SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11              block no longer exists
  util/qemu-openpty.c stub                   file no longer exists
  audio/audio_legacy.c                       file no longer exists
  configure feature-probe overrides          those features do exist at API 28

